  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1019 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nA shallow upper trough will move over the northern Great Plains on \nWednesday. The aforementioned ridge should shift just far enough to \nthe west to allow associated trailing shortwaves to have at least \nsome minor influence over the far southwestern Panhandle late-day. \nAs such, low-end PoPs have been retained in the latest forecast, \nalthough any storms should be confined to in and around the Friona \narea. Thursday and Friday will see more shortwave activity along the \neastern edge of the upper high. Highest storm chances look to mainly \noccur over the far southern Panhandle on Friday. Temperatures will \nslightly cool, but remain a few degrees above average in the mid 90s \non the Caprock and near 100 off the Caprock.",
